{
  "schema": "loom.address_syntax/1",
  "revision": 1,
  "calibration": true,
  "description": "Text syntaxes of a relative graph address (K3-1, R74/R76). The address itself is data (JSON steps); a syntax only says how it is written as text. Every token below is a preset, several syntaxes can exist at once, the parser and the printer take the one that is named. Everything concrete here is an example (the `default` grammar and the owner's alias are examples of what the engine must read and write); the list of syntaxes is open.",
  "default_syntax": "default",
  "syntaxes": {
    "default": {
      "kind": "preset",
      "label": { "pl": "Zapis domyślny", "en": "Default notation" },
      "why": {
        "pl": "Kroki oddzielone ukośnikiem, w kroku opcjonalna nazwa wymiaru i dwukropek, potem współrzędna: liczba (0 to bieżący węzeł, -1 poprzedni), liczba z kropką, nazwa w cudzysłowie, słowo (last, first, all), zakres (-3..0), poziomy (1.last.last), data i czas, warunek w nawiasach kwadratowych. To tylko przykład zapisu, nie wymaganie.",
        "en": "Steps separated by a slash; a step has an optional dimension name and a colon, then a coordinate: a number (0 is the current node, -1 the previous), a number with a dot, a quoted name, a word (last, first, all), a range (-3..0), levels (1.last.last), a date and time, a condition in square brackets. Only an example of a notation, not a requirement."
      },
      "tokens": {
        "step": "/",
        "dim": ":",
        "range": "..",
        "level": ".",
        "quote": "\"",
        "escape": "\\",
        "group_open": "(",
        "group_close": ")",
        "pred_open": "[",
        "pred_close": "]"
      },
      "datetime_pattern": "[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}(T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(:[0-9]{2}([.][0-9]+)?)?(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}(:?[0-9]{2})?)?)?",
      "aliases": [],
      "print_with_aliases": false,
      "examples": [
        { "text": "0", "canonical": "0" },
        { "text": "-1", "canonical": "-1" },
        { "text": "-1/version:last", "canonical": "-1/version:last" },
        { "text": "program_version:-1.last.last", "canonical": "program_version:-1.last.last" },
        { "text": "-3..0", "canonical": "-3..0" },
        { "text": "time:2026-10-22T10:00Z", "canonical": "time:2026-10-22T10:00Z" },
        { "text": "branch:prev/message:last", "canonical": "branch:prev/message:last" },
        { "text": "branch:\"main\"", "canonical": "branch:\"main\"" },
        { "text": "weight:0.5", "canonical": "weight:0.5" },
        { "text": "program_version:(1.2)", "canonical": "program_version:(1.2)" },
        { "text": "message:[role = \"user\"]", "canonical": "message:[role = \"user\"]" }
      ]
    },
    "owner_2026-10-23": {
      "kind": "example",
      "extends": "default",
      "label": { "pl": "Zapis z przykładu właściciela", "en": "Notation from the owner's example" },
      "why": {
        "pl": "Czyta skrót z jego słów: -1.\"00\" znaczy poprzednia wiadomość, jej wersja max.last. Właściciel sam napisał, że to tylko przykład składni, niekoniecznie dobry; drukujemy zawsze postać pełną -1/version:max.last.",
        "en": "Reads the shorthand from his words: -1.\"00\" means the previous message, its version max.last. The owner wrote himself that it is only an example of a syntax, not necessarily a good one; the full form -1/version:max.last is always printed."
      },
      "aliases": [
        {
          "id": "max_last",
          "match": ".\"00\"",
          "expands": "/version:max.last",
          "label": { "pl": "Skrót .\"00\"", "en": "Shorthand .\"00\"" },
          "why": {
            "pl": "Po współrzędnej oznacza: weź jej wersję max.last (najwyższa linia wersji, w niej ostatnia).",
            "en": "After a coordinate it means: take its version max.last (the highest version line, its last revision)."
          }
        }
      ],
      "print_with_aliases": false,
      "examples": [
        { "text": "-1.\"00\"", "canonical": "-1/version:max.last" },
        { "text": "-1/version:max.last", "canonical": "-1/version:max.last" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
